{"corrections":["Either repository: an open PR in analytics_toolkit or self_host should trigger the 30-minute maintenance orchestrator.\n\nForwarded by Codex from the owner’s actual chat answer, “Either repository (Recommended)”.\n\nQuestion: Should an open PR in either analytics_toolkit or self_host trigger the 30-minute orchestrator, or only an open analytics_toolkit PR?\nAnswer: Either repository (Recommended).","Scope clarification from the owner: “PR in self_host is considered relevant only if it affects github agents functionality”. An open analytics_toolkit PR qualifies; an open self_host PR qualifies only when it affects GitHub agent functionality. Preserve one orchestrator globally and the 30-minute cadence.\n\nTransparently forwarded by Codex from the owner’s actual latest chat message. This refines the earlier “Either repository (Recommended)” answer. It does not grant protected exact-head policy approval. For the remaining routine implementation options, use the previously requested independent plan resolver to check alignment with this scope.\n\nContext: https://github.com/Karapsin/analytics_toolkit/pull/26#issuecomment-6190878523","Accept \"Compatible companion first\" (Recommended), subject to the following fresh independent source-review corrections.\n\nCodex is posting this implementation-choice response under the owner's explicit standing authorization to answer agents in PRs and use independently checked recommended options. Fresh independent plan-resolution review by /root/review_notice_label_alignment accepted this choice. This is not a protected policy approval or a new owner fact, and does not approve the currently rejected source delta.\n\nPreserve the full maintenance objective, original task context, chronological questions and answers, and separately tracked PR-discovery dependency. Validate the actual controller producer-to-renderer contract with fast regressions, verify exact-commit GitHub checks, and obtain verified compatible companion activation evidence before enabling the controller payload change. Rendering tests alone do not prove outbound eligibility, Telegram delivery, or activation.\n\nAdditional fresh source-review findings for this exact head remain changes requested:\n\n1. tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py:155; docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md:97-98; companion agent_tools/tests/test_telegram_presentation.py:134,166-167\nNew assertions and documentation require agent:needs-user for a coordinator-owned provenance hold, although the patch itself says no new owner answer is needed. These positively codify the reported misleading state, beyond leaving unrelated legacy behavior unchanged.\nRequired correction: Keep the useful coordinator notice and renderer improvement and all private holds. Remove the new requirement that the legacy public label is correct. If retaining narrow notice scope, avoid newly prescribing that legacy label; truthful broader label mapping remains required. Preserve the test that owner policy approval cannot clear provenance holds.\n\n2. tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py:158-165; docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md:102\nThe new Owner cancelled the request. case requires an owner ping/resume as though an unanswered question existed. Cancellation is an actual owner decision stopping work.\nRequired correction: Remove cancellation from the owner-question contract and narrow blanket documentation. Preserve cancellation/veto enforcement; do not resume or infer consent.\n\nPreserve the existing native companion-compatibility finding and every private provenance hold, owner veto/cancellation, genuine authenticated owner question, exact-head approval, independent review and CI gate. Keep the useful incremental notice/renderer fix. Do not newly prescribe misleading public needs-user labels or treat cancellation as an unanswered question. Outbound notifications must continue to follow the owner's actual stated preference: user approvals/questions, Telegram-requested feature implementation status, merges with dev/main, and releases.\n\nFull actual review report retained as operator/pr29-fresh-source-alignment-report.json, SHA256 ada8c6cefe49fb7ddaf850360fac4b607182accb98ffcf86f4028ba54c1e9f47. No approval, CI success, runtime activation, or resolution of the current source rejection is claimed.","Use coordinated repository routing (Recommended), through a fresh ATK plan and independent plan review. The ATK correction worker has only ATK editable; do not claim an editable self_host workspace or treat older snapshots as current.\n\nCodex posts this routing response under the owner's standing authorization to reply to agents and resolve independently checked recommended implementation choices. Fresh independent resolver /root/review_notice_label_alignment approved this full-scope routing, superseding its earlier narrower interpretation. This is not a protected approval, new missing owner fact, provenance clearance or permission to narrow the feature.\n\nActual companion facts: self_host PR #15 merged as d0a34f3512de338d6d641568e9a95e1a7a863ca1. Worker 4e0db77e720d4df36dd1d0ed60a432402f266c0e (parent d0a34...) passed exact-commit GitHub Repository Checks run 38796620548, independent source/activation review and isolated rollout rehearsal; it is now deployed. The immutable full 44-path source map and activation proof are in operator/worker-prompt-paging-4e0db77e720d-active.json, SHA256 0664426e92a3755ca353596811e52b3f7f29839dc70f0d4fcf1106bef9f667a5, indexed by manifest.json's operator_companion_pin_receipt. Read that current source map and its exact source paths; do not assume the oldest companion directory is the active implementation. This proves the compatible renderer and prompt-size fix only. It does NOT prove outbound filtering or correction of the companion false-label tests.\n\nPreserve the full existing plan and original maintenance objective, task context and discovery dependency. After fresh planning and independent plan review, prepare the ATK notice/docs/tests corrections from the actual source review. The orchestrator, which has both repositories editable, owns ALL companion work below as explicitly pending work:\n\n1. Implement telegram.py outbound eligibility separately from rendering: suppress coordinator-only maintenance alerts; permit the owner-authorized categories of approvals/questions, Telegram-requested feature implementation status, merges with dev/main and releases.\n2. Preserve durable audit, retry and deduplication for eligible events. Suppressed events must be terminal and must not recur through retries.\n3. Add actual producer -> outbox -> renderer -> delivery regressions bound to immutable controller source. Rendering tests do not establish delivery behavior.\n4. Correct companion false-label tests/documentation; preserve provenance holds, owner veto/cancellation, genuine questions and exact-head approval gates.\n5. Obtain fresh independent review, exact-commit CI, isolated rehearsal and verified activation of the COMPLETE companion contract. Retain the cross-repository tooling-role repair as coordinator work rather than an owner fact request.\n\nATK merge, activation and paired-repair completion remain blocked until those full companion conditions have supporting evidence. ATK may prepare its own source after fresh plan/review, but must not claim the paired repair complete, enable the controller on rendering-only evidence, discard companion changes, or fabricate tool access. The existing source-review rejection remains actual feedback.\n\nThe complete current plan, actual workspace question, source/CI/activation identities, independently accepted routing and explicit dependency gate are retained for the next orchestrator in operator/pr29-role-workspace-scope-block.json, SHA256 1dc5f292a12f5cf7cd7e2127e06dba2b498fea7b84d00a5c480ff982828929be. No owner approval is posted here, and no missing source or delivery behavior is represented as supplied.","Accept both recommended implementation choices: (1) Explicit eligibility contract; (2) Route each question.\n\nCodex posts this reply under the owner's standing authorization to answer agents in PRs and select independently checked recommended options. Fresh independent resolver /root/review_notice_label_alignment approved both choices with the constraints below. This accepts implementation choices only; it supplies no missing owner fact, policy approval, provenance clearance or deployment approval.\n\nFor delivery, use additive metadata backed by verified host request bindings. Model inference and unverified payload fields cannot establish Telegram origin or permission to deliver. Allow only the owner-authorized notification categories. Reconcile legacy queued events against trusted authenticated state before delivery; never guess missing origin or default unresolved eligibility to delivery. Preserve durable audit, retry and deduplication for eligible events; suppressed maintenance events must be terminal and must not be resent.\n\nFor routing, preserve every original question and factual subquestion, including mixed clauses within ONE string. Route verified capability/evidence-access deficits internally while preserving genuine owner questions and all task context/checkpoints. Resume tooling-blocked work only after coordinator verification. Do not fabricate answers, clear unrelated holds, or bypass the authenticated paths for credentials, owner facts, veto/cancellation or protected approvals.\n\nRetain the COMPLETE existing paired repair gate: actual producer -> outbox -> renderer -> delivery regressions, companion filtering/legacy-queue handling, false-label test/docs corrections, independent review, exact-commit GitHub CI, isolated rehearsal and verified activation. Existing worker 4e0db77e720d4df36dd1d0ed60a432402f266c0e establishes rendering/paging only. ATK merge, activation and paired completion stay blocked until the full companion conditions are satisfied.\n\nUse a fresh ATK plan and independent plan review before preparing ATK source changes. The orchestrator owns all companion work and has both repositories editable; do not pretend this ATK-only worker has a companion write surface, drop that work, or route a coordinator capability deficit back to the owner. Preserve the full original feature objective and pending discovery/label dependencies. Record both actual questions and this answer together in task evidence."],"decisions":[],"images":[],"plans":[{"approval_index":null,"id":"7909883b12f921566b2345fb40f73d759d1358e3d64f4bc26033355b7a18c7b2","text":"# Complete PR #29 through coordinated repository routing\n\n## Summary and ownership\n\nPreserve the full maintenance objective, signed task context, chronological questions/answers and existing PR changes. After independent review of this revised plan, the ATK correction worker prepares only ATK changes. The orchestrator owns all companion changes in its separate writable self_host workspace.\n\nRetain independent recommendation resolution, one global maintenance agent at the 30-minute cadence, both-repository maintenance, and immediate exit when nothing needs fixing. Any open analytics_toolkit PR qualifies; self_host PRs qualify only when they affect GitHub agent functionality. Complete PR discovery remains a separately tracked dependency.\n\n## ATK corrections\n\n- Preserve `.github/agent/review_control.py`’s exact mismatch classification, coordinator guidance, deduplicated notice and additive `coordinator_blocked` field. Do not change recovery, provenance or approval authority.\n- In `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py`, remove the new assertion requiring `agent:needs-user` for a coordinator-owned provenance hold. Retain assertions for persisted reason/head, paused processing, no approval, notice deduplication and unrelated-label preservation.\n- Remove cancellation from the new owner-question parametrization. Keep genuine missing-input coverage and existing cancellation/veto enforcement. Preserve the test proving policy approval cannot clear a provenance hold.\n- Correct `docs/GITHUB_AGENT_OPERATIONS.md` and the changelog: remove endorsement of the legacy label and blanket owner-input wording; distinguish cancellation, coordinator recovery, rendering, delivery eligibility and activation.\n- Document the companion dependency explicitly. ATK source preparation is permitted after plan review; ATK merge, controller activation and paired-repair completion remain blocked pending the complete companion evidence below.\n\n## Orchestrator-owned companion work\n\nUse the current source map from `operator/worker-prompt-paging-4e0db77e720d-active.json`, revalidated against current self_host dev. Preserve merged PR #15 and subsequent runtime changes.\n\n- Retain the deployed compatible renderer and prompt-paging fix. Worker `4e0db77e720d4df36dd1d0ed60a432402f266c0e` already renders coordinator-blocked notices correctly; do not rebuild from the obsolete whole `3faf…` snapshot.\n- Implement outbound eligibility in companion `telegram.py`, independently of rendering. Permit owner approvals/questions, Telegram-requested feature implementation status, dev/main merges and releases. Suppress coordinator-only maintenance alerts.\n- Keep durable audit records. Eligible events retain retry, restart and deduplication behavior; suppressed events become terminal without Telegram calls or recurring retries.\n- Correct companion presentation tests/documentation that newly prescribe the misleading public label. Preserve private holds, genuine questions, cancellation/veto and exact-head approval gates.\n- Repair coordinator routing through the existing question-policy/intake/native-planning path: workspace capability and coordinator evidence-access deficits go to coordinator tooling work, preserving the complete task and checkpoints. Genuine missing owner facts, credentials and protected approvals must still reach the owner. This routing must not fabricate access or automatically answer those questions.\n\nThe notification interface remains additive and backward compatible. Missing/false `coordinator_blocked` retains legacy rendering behavior; rendering never establishes outbound eligibility.\n\n## Focused GitHub regressions\n\nUse temporary state and mocked GitHub/Telegram interactions; run no programs, tests, installs or rendering on the Pi.\n\n- Exercise actual controller producer → serialized outbox → renderer → delivery, covering maintenance and Telegram-feature branches. Bind the producer fixture to an immutable controller commit and content hash, and verify it matches the paired ATK implementation.\n- Cover coordinator wording, duplicate notices, unchanged private holds, genuine owner questions and policy approval’s inability to clear provenance holds.\n- Test each permitted notification category and suppression of coordinator-only maintenance alerts. Verify terminal suppression survives retries and restart.\n- Retain legacy payload, escaping/chunking, eligible-event retry and deduplication coverage.\n- Add routing regressions for the recorded workspace-capability question, mixed batches containing real owner questions, preserved checkpoints and unchanged security/approval boundaries.\n\n## Validation, activation and acceptance\n\n1. Independently review this revised plan before ATK implementation. Revalidate both repositories against current dev while preserving existing work.\n2. Obtain fresh companion source review, successful exact-commit Repository Checks and isolated rollout rehearsal for the **complete** delivery, test and routing contract.\n3. Activate that companion through trusted operations; record deployed revision/file hashes and preserved private state. Existing run `38796620548` and activation evidence establish renderer/paging support only.\n4. Require ATK final-head `fast-checks`, fresh independent review and authenticated owner exact-head protected approval. Do not merge or activate ATK until the complete companion dependency has verified activation evidence.\n5. Record paired acceptance separately from unresolved broader label mapping and PR discovery; neither is completed by this notice repair.\n\nPlanning is read-only against pinned dev `d319e72…`; startup sync was skipped, so findings may be stale. The current manifest has `fast_ci: []`, with no log paths to inspect. The coordinator owns fetching exact-head diagnostics. No edits or execution occurred, and no new approval or runtime completion is inferred.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"dc97447c145a5c2f95888677782301d7912502b6c9deaaa52885ebdc92a96053","text":"# Complete PR #29’s paired delivery and coordinator-routing repair\n\n## Summary and preserved objective\n\nPreserve existing PR changes and the complete maintenance feature: independent recommendation resolution, one global orchestrator every 30 minutes, maintenance across both repositories, immediate exit when nothing needs fixing, and no programs, tests, installs or rendering on the Pi. Any open analytics_toolkit PR qualifies; a self_host PR qualifies only when it affects GitHub agent functionality.\n\nApply the accepted **Explicit eligibility contract** and **Route each question** choices. Record both original questions and their chronological answer in task evidence. These choices grant no protected approval, provenance clearance or deployment approval.\n\nThe ATK worker prepares only ATK source after fresh independent plan review. The orchestrator owns all companion implementation and activation. Complete PR discovery and broader truthful label mapping remain separately tracked requirements.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n### ATK controller, tests and documentation\n\n- Preserve `.github/agent/review_control.py`’s exact mismatch classification, coordinator guidance, deduplicated notice, private provenance pause and additive `coordinator_blocked` field.\n- Add notification category and request-origin identifiers to relevant controller producers, including paused and routine rejection events. Treat these as lookup inputs; verified host state determines delivery eligibility. Branch names, model output and payload assertions cannot establish Telegram origin.\n- Preserve the existing corrections in `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py`: no new requirement for `agent:needs-user` on coordinator holds, cancellation excluded from owner-question coverage, and policy approval unable to clear provenance holds.\n- Update operations documentation and changelog to describe verified eligibility, legacy-queue handling, internal tooling routing and the complete activation gate accurately.\n\n### Companion delivery\n\nIn companion `telegram.py`, evaluate eligibility before rendering, stale-event retries or network calls:\n\n- Permit genuine owner approvals/questions, verified Telegram-requested feature implementation status, dev/main merges and releases.\n- Suppress coordinator-only maintenance events. A coordinator hold associated with a verified Telegram feature may remain eligible as feature status, while retaining coordinator wording and every private hold.\n- Validate feature origin through authenticated request records and their repository, request/revision and PR/head bindings. Extend intake-to-delivery wiring to expose this trusted lookup without exposing credentials.\n- Reconcile legacy queued events through trusted state. Unknown or conflicting eligibility remains durably held for coordinator reconciliation; it never defaults to delivery.\n- Persist suppression atomically using the existing outbox’s terminal state plus an audit disposition and reason. Retain the original event and deduplication key; create no delivery receipt or Telegram message. Suppressed events must remain terminal across restart and duplicate enqueue.\n- Preserve eligible-event durable rendering, chunk progress, retries, callbacks and deduplication.\n\nRetain the deployed compatible renderer and prompt paging. Missing/false `coordinator_blocked` continues legacy presentation; it does not grant delivery eligibility. No public package API change or notification-table migration is required.\n\n### Companion question routing\n\nExtend the shared question policy and existing intake/native-planning path:\n\n- Retain every original question verbatim. Track routing dispositions separately for each question and factual clause, including mixed clauses within one string.\n- Route verified workspace-capability and coordinator evidence-access deficits internally. Preserve genuine owner questions in mixed batches and mixed strings.\n- Keep uncertain factual clauses unresolved. Credentials, owner facts, veto/cancellation, original evidence and protected approvals retain their authenticated handling.\n- Persist tooling blockers and checkpoints. Resume affected work only after coordinator verification of the repaired capability/evidence access, with all other holds still enforced.\n- Preserve independent resolver review for routine recommendations; routing cannot supply answers or approve a plan.\n\nCorrect companion presentation tests and documentation that prescribe the misleading public label. Retain producer coverage, persisted holds, genuine questions and approval protections.\n\n## Focused fast regression coverage\n\nRun service-free tests on GitHub with temporary databases and mocked GitHub/Telegram:\n\n- Actual controller producer → serialized outbox → renderer → delivery, covering maintenance and Telegram-feature branches. Pin controller fixture source by commit and content hash; fail on divergence from the paired implementation.\n- Every permitted category; suppressed maintenance; forged origin metadata; missing/conflicting request bindings; legacy queued events; and unresolved eligibility without network calls.\n- Terminal suppression across retry, restart and duplicate enqueue; eligible-event retry, chunk continuation and deduplication.\n- Coordinator wording, duplicate notices, unchanged holds, genuine owner questions, cancellation/veto enforcement and policy approval’s inability to clear provenance holds.\n- The recorded workspace request, mixed batches, mixed clauses within one string, preserved original text/checkpoints, verified tooling recovery, and unchanged credential/approval boundaries.\n- Existing renderer compatibility, escaping, chunking, resolver alignment and orchestrator singleton/cadence behavior.\n\nUse companion presentation, intake/native-planning and worker-role suites alongside ATK repository regressions. Include the isolated rollout rehearsal in companion Repository Checks.\n\n## GitHub validation, activation and completion\n\n1. Independently review this revised plan. Revalidate against current dev in both repositories while preserving existing work.\n2. Start from the active companion’s exact source map, preserving merged PR #15 and subsequent runtime changes. Worker `4e0db77…` and run `38796620548` establish rendering/paging only.\n3. Obtain fresh independent companion source review, successful exact-commit Repository Checks and isolated rollout rehearsal for the complete filtering, legacy-queue, routing and test contract.\n4. Activate through trusted operations. Record deployed revision/file hashes, verified request-binding wiring, delivery behavior and preservation of private state, checkpoints and schedules.\n5. Require final-head ATK `fast-checks`, fresh independent review and authenticated owner exact-head protected approval. ATK merge, controller activation and paired completion remain blocked until the complete companion activation evidence exists.\n6. Record paired acceptance separately from pending discovery and broader label mapping; preserve those dependencies until independently completed.\n\n## Evidence limits\n\nPlanning used pinned dev `d319e72a09cb376fcb3fbe81bbefadadf80f1c90`; startup synchronization was skipped, so findings may be stale. No edits or execution occurred.\n\nThe inspected manifest has `fast_ci: []`, so no assigned diagnostic logs are available. Supplied successful jobs for ATK head `bb5235df…` do not establish the aggregate `fast-checks` result or validate a future head. The coordinator owns obtaining exact-head checks and any required logs; no owner log request is needed.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"3aeb5ef1744c164287bfca824032477f836606ae5e7acdc2a0e119a4e87a260f","text":"# Complete PR #29 against current dev\n\n## Summary and established scope\n\nPreserve PR #29’s notice and notification-metadata improvements while reconciling them onto pinned dev `5b3b02d1a9c2afa93b6d0d4a1eac7dbfc03b828b`. Obtain independent review of this fresh plan before coding.\n\nThe chronological answers resolve the material scope questions:\n\n- Independently assess recommended choices against the complete request; recommendations alone grant no approval.\n- Keep one global orchestrator, scheduled every 30 minutes, with access to both repositories and immediate exit when nothing needs fixing.\n- Any open analytics_toolkit PR qualifies. A self_host PR qualifies only when it affects GitHub agent functionality.\n- Preserve complete PR discovery and truthful label mapping as separately tracked dependencies.\n- Keep all original questions, answers, verification records, prior plans and checkpoints.\n\nNo additional owner answer is required. Companion implementation and operational work remain coordinator-owned; the ATK worker must not claim a writable self_host workspace.\n\n## ATK implementation\n\nReconcile the existing feature onto current dev rather than replacing current files with the older branch versions.\n\n- In `.github/agent/review_control.py`, retain dev’s status reconciliation, coordinator holds and renewal replay protection, amendment handling, authenticated recovery and notification suppression.\n- Reapply the exact task-context-mismatch classification, deduplicated coordinator notice and additive `coordinator_blocked` field. The notice must request coordinator verification without implying owner input, automatic recovery or approval.\n- Preserve additive `notification_category` and `request_origin` metadata for pause, reviewer-rejection and approval producers. Branch and optional task digest remain lookup hints; they cannot establish authenticated origin or delivery permission.\n- Retain the corrected notice/hold cases in `tests/repository/label_reconciliation.py` and metadata cases in `tests/repository/notification_metadata.py`. Preserve dev’s shared fakes and existing concurrency expectations.\n- Merge the relevant operations documentation and changelog additions without removing newer dev documentation or historical entries. Distinguish coordinator recovery, genuine owner questions, cancellation, rendering, delivery and activation.\n\nNo public package API or database migration is planned. Existing event keys, callback authentication and legacy rendering compatibility remain intact.\n\n## Companion compatibility and paired validation\n\nThe supplied immutable source and activation history support delivery filtering, clause routing and source-paired regressions beyond the historical rendering-only repair. The current supplied runtime pin is `bfb4ba70ff85369292d347ab60a840d9bed133f6`; its history retains the `05d5b826…` delivery repair.\n\nThose regressions pin PR #29’s older producer, whose module hash matches the inspected candidate. They do not validate the future controller reconciled with dev.\n\nThe orchestrator must therefore:\n\n- Refresh `agent_tools/tests/fixtures/pr29_notification_producer.json` and `test_current_notification_delivery.py` against the final immutable ATK controller commit and module hash. Preserve historical fixtures.\n- Exercise the actual producer → SQLite outbox → trusted eligibility → renderer → delivery path using the reconciled controller’s current authority behavior.\n- Preserve eligibility checks before rendering and every network send, terminal maintenance suppression, durable unresolved-event holds, legacy/partial-queue reconciliation, and eligible retry/deduplication.\n- Allow only authenticated owner approvals/questions, verified Telegram-requested feature status, dev/main merges and releases. Null or absent optional hints may derive only from matching private bindings; conflicting hints remain unresolved.\n- Preserve clause-level routing and original question text, including mixed strings. Resume tooling-blocked work only after coordinator verification; retain authenticated handling for credentials, owner facts, cancellation/veto and protected approvals.\n\nChange companion production code only if this refreshed pairing exposes an in-scope incompatibility. Rendering compatibility alone cannot satisfy the dependency.\n\n## Focused fast regressions\n\nRun validation on GitHub with temporary state and mocked GitHub/Telegram; execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering on the Pi.\n\nCover:\n\n- Coordinator wording, duplicate notices, persisted provenance holds and unrelated-label preservation.\n- Genuine owner questions; cancellation/veto enforcement; policy approval unable to clear provenance or coordinator holds.\n- Every permitted notification category, forged metadata, null/missing/conflicting bindings and legacy events.\n- Terminal suppression without network calls or new delivery receipts, surviving restart and duplicate enqueue.\n- Eligible retry, chunk continuation, stale-head rejection and exact-head approval buttons.\n- Mixed question batches and clauses, preserved checkpoints, verified tooling recovery and unchanged independent-resolver boundaries.\n- Existing dev coordinator-renewal replay, owner-attention/status reconciliation, scoped merge and publication/archive regressions affected by reconciliation.\n- Existing singleton, 30-minute cadence, qualifying-PR discovery and no-work termination coverage.\n\n## GitHub and completion gates\n\n1. Independently review this plan, then revalidate against current dev while preserving existing work.\n2. Publish the signed successor with complete chronological task evidence. Obtain fresh independent source review and successful final-head aggregate `fast-checks`.\n3. Obtain exact-commit companion Repository Checks, independent compatibility review and isolated rehearsal for the refreshed pairing. Verify the activated runtime retains that complete contract and private state.\n4. Retain the request-bound dependency barrier until coordinator verification accepts the final paired evidence. Archived receipts cannot clear unrelated holds or transfer approval.\n5. Require authenticated owner exact-head protected approval before ATK merge and trusted controller activation. Verify the deployed controller revision and paired behavior before recording completion.\n6. Report remaining discovery and broader label dependencies separately.\n\nThe supplied checks show `fast-checks` succeeded for historical head `7e9770db…`, while `agent-review` failed. Neither result validates a successor. The manifest contains no `fast_ci` logs; the coordinator obtains any final-head diagnostics.\n\nPlanning was read-only against the pinned snapshot, without startup synchronization; live state may have advanced. No edits, execution, approval or deployment occurred.\n"}],"producer_id":"orchestrator:da19e8b1a06943ecbd66227a4bd1c89f","questions":[{"answer_index":2,"id":"4d976dc07b219bce7e3fc9ddefd8b0f07db3f45e3eae3e8cc054ee2ddfa18d70","text":"1. Compatibility repair: should we preserve PR #29 and add the companion renderer support, testing the actual controller payload and verifying companion activation before enabling the controller change? This preserves the full maintenance objective and its separately tracked discovery dependency; it grants no protected approval.\nCompatible companion first (Recommended): Add coordinator-blocked rendering, fast controller-to-renderer regressions, exact-commit GitHub validation and activation evidence before controller rollout."},{"answer_index":3,"id":"11ab2333bbb6dc9f54795f012b698de9dfafad7dfe2ce37aed287fe31a8050cd","text":"Can the coordinator expose an editable self_host companion workspace through source_files, with immutable source for PR #15 head 1874278af6268538491cf066d703a91e10b9ccff, base e72023bed122aae0db8a8b628ca62aa28586043a and matching CI evidence? The reviewed plan requires preserving and correcting that companion, but this worker exposes only analytics_toolkit source and older read-only companion snapshots."},{"answer_index":4,"id":"9797d4e7306bac0d46fc8070a2c64e9693d2e9de912416a960264b5ea9cf804b","text":"1. Delivery contract: should the paired repair add trusted notification-category/request-origin metadata so transport can distinguish Telegram feature status from coordinator-only maintenance, including task-context mismatch events whose current payload omits branch/request identity?\nExplicit eligibility contract (Recommended): Use additive producer metadata and verified host request bindings; allow only the stated owner categories, terminally audit suppressed maintenance events, and reconcile legacy queued events from trusted state before delivery. Preserve legacy rendering, holds and approvals.\n\n2. Coordinator routing: should the repair classify workspace-capability/evidence-access deficits separately in mixed question batches, preserving genuine owner questions and resuming only after the coordinator verifies the tooling repair?\nRoute each question (Recommended): Extend shared question policy and intake/native-planning routing; retain complete questions, task context and checkpoints, route tooling items internally, and keep credentials, owner facts, veto/cancellation and protected approvals on their existing authenticated paths."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"for \"ALWAYS use reccomended\" let's just spawn \"plan resolver\" agent on RPI which checks that recommended options and if they are aligned with user request -approves them. Also add \"orchestrator\" agent which is spawned every 30 minutes (no more than 1 such agent) IF at least 1 PR is open and  it basically does what you do now: finds issues in rpi agents toolkit, fixes them, etc. still no heavy checks on rpi. but it may edit atk and self host dirs. If nothng to fix - that agent ceases to exist","task_id":"orchestrator:da19e8b1a06943ecbd66227a4bd1c89f","version":2}